facts.quote:
There are exceptions from all prohibitions in the Regulations relating to:
 Payments relating to designated persons relating to prior contracts;
 Pension payments;
 Diplomatic missions and international organizations;
 Prior funds held by a designated person belonging to a Canadian;
 Legal services for a designated person;
 Loan repayments;

There are exceptions from the prohibition on restricted goods and industrial goods relating to:
 Temporary media exports;
 International nuclear safeguards verification;
 The Government of Canada;
 The Chemical Weapons Convention;
 The International Space Station;
 Software updates;
 Civil aircraft;
 Aircraft and ship stores;
 Maintenance, repair or operation of aircraft of Canadian and US air carriers;
 Consumer communication devices;
 Personal effects.
